From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edk2-cix <edk2-cix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:48:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/CIX/Sky1: PdDxe: skip unassigned PD alert pins

Boards with fewer than four PD controllers mark the unused slots with
0xFF.  Do not register GPIO 255 as an alert interrupt for such slots.

From Neol00/edk2-cix-unlocked V2.4.
---
 Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PdDxe/PdDxe.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PdDxe/PdDxe.c b/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PdDxe/PdDxe.c
index 8e97b8e7..400cb37a 100644
--- a/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PdDxe/PdDxe.c
+++ b/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PdDxe/PdDxe.c
@@ -319,6 +319,13 @@ SortEnabledAlertPin (
       continue;
     }
 
+    //
+    // 0xFF marks an unassigned alert pin (no PD controller in that slot).
+    //
+    if (PdDevList[i].AlertPin == 0xFF) {
+      continue;
+    }
+
     for (j = 0; j < SortedCnt; j++) {
       if (PdDevList[i].AlertPin == AlertPins[j]) {
         break;
